From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: report NSS RSA failure without crashing

The complete upstream tcwiki test crashes just after its HMAC assertions on
the target openEuler RISC-V image. The NSS RSA signer can return NULL on an
error, but tcwiki passes that pointer to strcmp unconditionally. Report the
NSPR error at the signer and fail the same test normally when signing did not
produce a signature. This diagnostic does not skip any test or turn a failed
RSA assertion into success.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI runs 36432105235 and 36433796200.
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Remove-When: Upstream reports NSS signer failures and guards the test result.
---
 src/hash.c             | 2 ++
 tests/selftest_wiki.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hash.c b/src/hash.c
--- a/src/hash.c
+++ b/src/hash.c
@@ -99,4 +99,5 @@
 #include "pk11pub.h"
 #include "nss.h"
+#include "prerror.h"
 #include "base64.h"
 #include "keyhi.h"
@@ -219,2 +220,3 @@ char *oauth_sign_rsa_sha1 (const char *m, const char *k) {
 looser:
+  if (!rv) fprintf(stderr, "liboauth/NSS: RSA-SHA1 signer failed (NSPR error %d)\n", PR_GetError());
   if (pkey) SECKEY_DestroyPrivateKey(pkey);
diff --git a/tests/selftest_wiki.c b/tests/selftest_wiki.c
--- a/tests/selftest_wiki.c
+++ b/tests/selftest_wiki.c
@@ -147 +147 @@ int main (int argc, char **argv) {
-  if (strcmp(b64d,"jvTp/wX1TYtByB1m+Pbyo0lnCOLIsyGCH7wke8AUs3BpnwZJtAuEJkvQL2/9n4s5wUmUl4aCI4BwpraNx4RtEXMe5qg5T1LVTGliMRpKasKsW//e+RinhejgCuzoH26dyF8iY2ZZ/5D1ilgeijhV/vBka5twt399mXwaYdCwFYE=")) {
+  if (!b64d || strcmp(b64d,"jvTp/wX1TYtByB1m+Pbyo0lnCOLIsyGCH7wke8AUs3BpnwZJtAuEJkvQL2/9n4s5wUmUl4aCI4BwpraNx4RtEXMe5qg5T1LVTGliMRpKasKsW//e+RinhejgCuzoH26dyF8iY2ZZ/5D1ilgeijhV/vBka5twt399mXwaYdCwFYE=")) {
